","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"The inner keep: Hell's corner","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Hammering home the cork","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"\"Count your children now, Adolf!\"","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Tunisgrad","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Epilogue.","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}}],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"The liberation of Europe and defeat of the Third Reich is an epic story of courage and calamity, of miscalculation and enduring triumph. Sixty years after America joined the struggle, Atkinson shows why no modern reader can understand the Allied victory without a grasp of what unfolded in North Africa in 1942-943, where American officers learned how to lead, soldiers learned how to hate, and an army learned what it takes to vanquish a formidable enemy."},"series":["The Liberation trilogy -- volume one","Thorndike Press large print nonfiction","Thorndike Press large print nonfiction series"],"local_id":["urn:sfpl:31223106430276","urn:sfpl:31223106337646","urn:sfpl:31223106337620","urn:bwbsku:W7-BXX-360"],"full_title":"An army at dawn the war in North Africa, 1942-1943","lc_classifications":["D766.82 .A82 2013"],"key":"/books/OL27152437M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL713435A"}],"subtitle":"the war in North Africa, 1942-1943","subjects":["Campaigns","Large type books","Operation Torch, 1942","World War, 1939-1945","Military History"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"pagination":"987 pages (large print)","source_records":["marc:marc_openlibraries_sanfranciscopubliclibrary/sfpl_chq_2018_12_24_run04.mrc:377612306:4835","marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part40.utf8:229310359:1251","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2022-08-13"],"title":"An army at dawn","dewey_decimal_class":["940.54/23"],"notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Originally published: New York : Henry Holt and Co., 2002.\n\nIncludes bibliographical references (pages 907-976)."},"number_of_pages":987,"isbn_13":["9781594136900","9781410463210"],"edition_name":"Large print edition.","lccn":["2013024466"],"subject_places":["North Africa"],"isbn_10":["1594136904","1410463214"],"publish_date":"2013","publish_country":"miu","copyright_date":"2002","by_statement":"Rick Atkinson","oclc_numbers":["849822665"],"works":[{"key":"/works/OL3918091W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"latest_revision":6,"revision":6,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2019-07-18T05:49:23.574380"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2022-12-04T18:08:59.393559"}},{"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"title":"An Army at Dawn","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL713435A"}],"publish_date":"May 15, 2007","source_records":["amazon:1429967633","bwb:9781429967631"],"number_of_pages":704,"publishers":["Henry Holt and Co."],"isbn_10":["1429967633"],"isbn_13":["9781429967631"],"physical_format":"digital","full_title":"An Army at Dawn The War in North Africa, 1942-1943, Volume One of the Liberation Trilogy","subtitle":"The War in North Africa, 1942-1943, Volume One of the Liberation Trilogy","notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Source title: An Army at Dawn: The War in North Africa, 1942-1943, Volume One of the Liberation Trilogy"},"works":[{"key":"/works/OL3918091W"}],"key":"/books/OL31977434M","latest_revision":5,"revision":5,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2021-02-21T03:06:19.828620"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2021-12-30T15:56:22.706535"}},{"works":[{"key":"/works/OL3918091W"}],"title":"Un ejército al amanecer","publishers":["Crítica"],"publish_date":"2014","key":"/books/OL36348706M","type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"identifiers":{},"covers":[12506326],"classifications":{},"physical_dimensions":"22 x 14.5 x  centimeters","series":["Memoria Crítica"],"number_of_pages":736,"translated_from":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"physical_format":"Tapa blanda con solapas","description":"Este libro, galardonado con el Premio Pulitzer de Historia 2003, ha sido considerado por el *Wall Street Journal* como el mejor relato sobre la segunda guerra mundial, desde las obras clásicas de Cornelius Ryan *El día más largo* y *Un puente demasiado lejano*. La liberación de Europa y la destrucción del Tercer Reich es una historia épica de valor y sufrimiento, de aciertos, errores y de triunfo final. Pero ningún lector de nuestros días puede entender la victoria de los Aliados sin partir del inmenso drama que se desarrolló en el norte de Africa en 1942 y 1943. El relato de Atkinson comienza con la operación «Antorcha» y la lucha inicial contra los franceses para proseguir con el enfrentamiento de las tropas aliadas con el ejército alemán. En aquel escenario terrible fue donde aquéllas aprendieron el coste de vencer a un enemigo formidable y donde se forjaron la mayoría de los grandes generales de la segunda guerra mundial como Eisenhower, Patton, Bradley o Montgomery frente a guerreros tan prestigiosos como Rommel o Kesselring. Pero más allá de los grandes nombres, Atkinson nos conduce hasta la primera línea de fuego donde el combate, la muerte en las trincheras y las anónimas tragedias comunes a todas las guerras nos muestran el rostro profundamente humano de una batalla crucial para el destino de la civilización.","subtitle":"La guerra en el norte de África, 1942-1943","contributors":[{"name":"Marcelo Covián","role":"Translator"}],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/spa"}],"translation_of":"An Army at Dawn","publish_places":["Barcelona"],"isbn_13":["9788498927634"],"isbn_10":["8498927633"],"latest_revision":5,"revision":5,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2021-12-30T15:46:24.400416"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2021-12-30T15:56:22.706535"}},{"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Este libro, galardonado con el Premio Pulitzer de Historia 2003, ha sido considerado por el Wall Street Journal como el mejor relato sobre la segunda guerra mundial, desde las obras clásicas de Cornelius Ryan *El día más largo* y *Un puente demasiado lejano*.\r\n\r\nLa liberación de Europa y la destrucción del Tercer Reich es una historia épica de valor y sufrimiento, de aciertos, errores y de triunfo final. Pero ningún lector de nuestros días puede entender la victoria de los Aliados sin partir del inmenso drama que se desarrolló en el norte de Africa en 1942 y 1943.\r\n\r\nEl relato de Atkinson comienza con la operación «Antorcha» y la lucha inicial contra los franceses para proseguir con el enfrentamiento de las tropas aliadas con el ejército alemán. En aquel escenario terrible fue donde aquéllas aprendieron el coste de vencer a un enemigo formidable y donde se forjaron la mayoría de los grandes generales de la segunda guerra mundial como Eisenhower, Patton, Bradley o Montgomery frente a guerreros tan prestigiosos como Rommel o Kesselring. Pero más allá de los grandes nombres, Atkinson nos conduce hasta la primera línea de fuego donde el combate, la muerte en las trincheras y las anónimas tragedias comunes a todas las guerras nos muestran el rostro profundamente humano de una batalla crucial para el destino de la civilización.\r\n\r\n*Un ejército al amanecer* se convertirá en un clásico de la historia militar y de los estudios de estrategia. Atkinson escribe con increíble perspicacia y maestría sobre los detalles cotidianos sin perder nunca de vista el panorama general. Sin perder un solo detalle, nos lleva desde la más alta política hasta el fondo de la trinchera más miserable."},"notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Incluye ilustraciones y mapas."},"identifiers":{"goodreads":["417866"],"librarything":["13178"]},"title":"Un ejército al amanecer","subtitle":"La guerra en el norte de África, 1942-1943","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL713435A"}],"publish_date":"2004","publishers":["Crítica"],"weight":"2.8 pounds","covers":[14313772],"physical_format":"Tapa dura","subjects":["Military - General","History - Military / War"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/spa"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"physical_dimensions":"9.3 x 7.1 x 1.8 inches","pagination":"703 p., [32] p. de lám. 1 mapa","translation_of":"An Army at Dawn: The War in North Africa, 1942-1943","publish_places":["Barcelona"],"translated_from":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"isbn_10":["8484325210"],"isbn_13":["9788484325215"],"oclc_numbers":["433630248"],"source_records":["amazon:8484325210"],"key":"/books/OL13324090M","number_of_pages":703,"works":[{"key":"/works/OL3918091W"}],"latest_revision":14,"revision":14,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-30T20:50:18.033121"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2026-01-31T22:46:50.687223"}},{"identifiers":{"goodreads":["3185629"]},"title":"Army at Dawn","subtitle":"The War in North Africa, 1942-1943 (Liberation Trilogy)","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL713435A"}],"publish_date":"October 2003","publishers":["Tandem Library"],"physical_format":"Unknown Binding","isbn_13":["9781417723447"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"isbn_10":["1417723440"],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"subjects":["Military - World War II","History - Military / War"],"first_sentence":{"type":"/type/text","value":"A FEW minutes past 10 A.M. on Wednesday, October 21, 1942, a twin-engine Navy passenger plane broke through the low overcast blanketing Washington, D.C., then banked over the Potomac River for the final approach to Anacostia Field."},"source_records":["amazon:1417723440"],"key":"/books/OL9427916M","works":[{"key":"/works/OL3918091W"}],"latest_revision":5,"revision":5,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-30T09:38:13.731961"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2026-02-14T01:39:28.702621"}}]}